# Set Loiter Rad writes LOITER_RAD or WP_LOITER_RAD - and on a copter, which has neither, nothing.
#
# modifyandSetLoiterRad_Click calls setParam(new[] {"LOITER_RAD", "WP_LOITER_RAD"}, value), which
# writes the first name the vehicle has and returns false, silently, when it has none. ArduCopter
# has neither, so the product path on this SITL is the refusal - asserted only after the parameters
# are downloaded, so the answer comes from the vehicle's own list rather than an empty one.
# `GCSViews/FlightData.cs:4412-4424, ExtLibs/ArduPilot/Mavlink/MAVLinkInterface.cs:1609-1650`
#
# Needs SITL (a copter): tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-loiterrad.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen params
window 1600x1200
settle 6

click param-download
settle 15
expect params.held > 500

click tab-fly
settle 1

# The Actions grid is on the Actions page, tabActions; the strip opens on Quick, as
# tabControlactions.SelectedIndex = 0 has it. `GCSViews/FlightData.Designer.cs:595-611`
click fly-tab-actions
expect fly.tab tabActions
click fly-loiterrad-value
key ctrl+u
type 80
# Keystrokes reach the application through the input method (ibus, over XIM) and come back
# after a round trip; a click does not. Settle, so the click cannot overtake the typing.
settle 1
click fly-setloiterrad
expect fly.sent nothing: neither LOITER_RAD nor WP_LOITER_RAD is on this vehicle
